 "_doc": "The voice decider's explicit overrides (voice_decider/rules.rs), checked before the model: they always win. Matched on the utterance lowercased, accents and punctuation (but « ? ») taken out. Order: stop > go > (v2 package: an explicit end of the call, `goodbye_explicit` → raccrocher, a bare goodbye left to the model; 4-label package:) a goodbye (`goodbye`, at most 3 words before it, a `goodbye_after` word after it, the agent's name left out: the call's own goodbye check hangs up on a whole one first) > the agent's name + a question > note > an answer to the Bip's question (`agent_asked`: the Bip's last line asked something, this is the first pause since) unless it holds on (`answer_hold`: wait, reading, practice); a real question only (4 words at least, not a check-in like « Oui ? » or « How can I help? »), and only with a 4-label package (the v2 model reads the Bip's line). The lists of research/voice-decider/rules.py (branch voice-decider-spike), where they were measured: right at 100 % on the hand-written core set when they fire. After the model (12/11, « Hello, ça va ? » was held): a hold on a short whole utterance (`closed_words_max` words at most, not ending on « , » « … » or an `open_end` word) that is a greeting alone (`greeting`, not with the agent's name: that calls the Bip), a check-in (`closed_forms`) or a greeting + a question ending in « ? » → lancer, when nothing waits (VoiceDeciderRules.closedShort, Rules.closedShort, rules_v2.closed_short).",
